  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_05. Let triangle ABC be a triangle with sides AB = 14, BC = 16, AC = 10. Let triangle MNP be a triangle with sides MN = 8, NP = 7, MP = 5. Let segment MN be a midsegment segment. Let segment NP be a midsegment segment. Let segment MP be a midsegment segment. Segment MN is parallel to BC. Segment NP is parallel to AB. Segment MP is parallel to AC. Segment MNP is a midsegment parallel to ABC and half its length. Find the length of MN.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A triangular plot of land ABC has sides measuring AB = 14 meters, BC = 16 meters, and AC = 10 meters. A surveyor marks the midpoints of two sides and connects them with a segment MN, creating a smaller triangle MNP by also connecting the midpoints of the remaining sides.\n\nThe three segments MN, NP, and MP each connect midpoints of the original triangle's sides. This means:\n- Segment MN is parallel to side BC\n- Segment NP is parallel to side AB  \n- Segment MP is parallel to side AC\n\nBecause triangle MNP is formed entirely by connecting midpoints, it is a dilation of triangle ABC with a scale factor of 1/2, centered at one of the vertices. This dilation relationship guarantees that each side of the smaller triangle is parallel to and exactly half the length of the corresponding side in the original triangle.\n\nGiven that the sides of triangle MNP measure MN = 8 meters, NP = 7 meters, and MP = 5 meters, what is the length of MN?"
}